ready: 1
kind: system
id: sys.daemon
name: Kernle daemon
role: The single writer of stack databases while it runs; schedules sleep, retention, and sync, ingests transcripts, and keeps the search index and embedding model warm
system_kind: service
hosting: launchd user agent on macOS, systemd user service on Linux
code: crates/kernled
responsibilities:
  - Serializes writes to each stack
  - Runs scheduled sleep, retention, and sync
  - Ingests runtime transcripts
  - Holds the warm search index and embedding model
connections:
  - to: sys.home
    label: Reads and writes stacks
  - to: sys.model
    label: Appraisal judging and extraction during sleep
  - to: sys.cloud
    label: Push and pull changes for synced stacks
  - to: sys.claude-code
    label: Reads session transcripts
  - to: sys.codex
    label: Reads session files
units:
  - name: scheduler
    unit_kind: schedule
    schedule: Debounced after activity, nightly sleep, daily retention, periodic sync
